---
description: Never add Co-authored-by or similar AI/tool attribution trailers
alwaysApply: true
---

# No coauthor / attribution trailers

Never add any of the following to git commits, PRs, file headers, or docs:

- `Co-authored-by:` / `Co-Authored-By:`
- Cursor, Claude, Copilot, or other AI/tool identity as author or coauthor
- `Generated-by:`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or similar attribution footers

Commit messages are the user's voice only (name/email from their git config).

If a tool injects `--trailer Co-authored-by:…` into `git commit` (Cursor does this),
do not leave it. Rewrite the tip with `git commit-tree` / `git update-ref` so the
published message has no coauthor trailer — never amend by re-running `git commit`
without stripping, or the trailer comes back.
